            <p>To the breathtaking desert scenery - crystal clear, as the ocean water & Kali ganas hiking trail on the sea. As the boat glides toward the southernmost tip of the Baja Peninsula, you are greeted by the world-famous Arch of Cabo San Lucas hanging over gold and soft sand beaches that fade into an infinite horizon. The premises, too, are grand and cinematic, a setup that builds anticipation before you even hit the shore. </p>

            <p>Arriving by sea gives you a different dimension, especially considering how much Los Cabos has been shaped by the nautical ethos. A busy harbor, alive with fishing boats and yachts, and cruise ships moored offshore. A cruise to Los Cabos is a blissful experience that provides travellers with an opportunity to sit back and thoroughly enjoy one of Mexico's most beautiful coastal areas, intermixed with sightseeing. </p>

            <h2>Waves of the Los Cabos Region and Coastal Adventures</h2>

            <p>A Los Cabos cruise typically has a stop in Cabo San Lucas, where tourists have the option to browse dozens of local markets and enjoy restaurants literally on the water or at beautiful beaches. The town strikes a balance between luxury resorts and the traditional, all of which can cater to every type of traveller. From the promenade along the marina, colourful boats and alluring ocean vistas lie before you. </p>

            <p>On land, activities may consist of snorkelling in aquamarine water or touring unspoiled bays or desert footpaths. The countryside contrasts deep blue water, jagged cliffs and sandy shores. A cruise to Los Cabos is a holistic trip of adventure and relaxation. </p>

